From 13698ecfc32076c4088c238c6bfb3f30d01a6ee6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexaInc <rasanjanahansaka2006@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:20:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(firmware): reliable ESP32-CAM capture with retries,
 precise fault reporting

- Capture trigger hardened: up to 3 attempts, each preceded by a forced 25ms
  UART idle gap so the standalone 'C' always satisfies the CAM smart-trigger
  rule even when a previous debug line was corrupted on the shared UART0.
- Per-attempt 3s header timeout (8s restored for the JPEG body), so a dead
  link fails fast instead of one blind 8s wait.
- <IMG:0> from the CAM is now understood as 'camera not ready' (init failed /
  power / ribbon) and reported distinctly from a dead UART link.
- Every capture failure now: prints a hardware checklist to the log, shows a
  15s 'CAM ERROR! CHECK CAM' banner on the JMD0.96D-1 status screen, and
  sends a camera_fault message that the server turns into a dashboard alert.
- ESP32-CAM sketch: replies <IMG:0> instead of staying silent when the camera
  is not ready or returns an empty frame, and retries esp_camera_init on the
  next trigger (boot brownouts often clear).
- arduino-ide README: camera timeout troubleshooting checklist (5V power,
  crossed TX0/RX0 wiring, GPIO0 flash-mode pin, USB serial monitor contention,
  matched 921600 baud).
- Applied identically to src/main.cpp, sketch.ino and the arduino-ide
  sketches; Wokwi firmware.bin/.elf rebuilt (pio run SUCCESS).
